-- Seed Cognitive Enhancement Course Template with full 56-day lesson content
-- Unique: NO INJECTIONS - Uses nasal sprays only

UPDATE course_templates
SET 
  duration_days = 56,
  peptides = '[
    {
      "name": "Semax",
      "purpose": "Cognitive enhancement and focus",
      "dosing_research": "200mcg daily (Weeks 1-2), then 400mcg daily (Weeks 3-8)",
      "timing": "Morning (has mild stimulating effect)",
      "frequency": "Once daily",
      "site": "Nasal spray - no injection required",
      "notes": "Nootropic peptide that increases BDNF. NO NEEDLES."
    },
    {
      "name": "Selank",
      "purpose": "Anxiety reduction and calm focus",
      "dosing_research": "250mcg daily (Weeks 1-2), then 500mcg daily (Weeks 3-8)",
      "timing": "Morning or as needed for anxiety",
      "frequency": "Once daily",
      "site": "Nasal spray - no injection required",
      "notes": "Anxiolytic nootropic that modulates GABA. NO NEEDLES."
    }
  ]'::jsonb,
  lessons = '[
    {"day": 0, "phase": "Introduction", "title": "Welcome to Your Cognitive Enhancement Course", "content": "Welcome to the Cognitive Enhancement Course. Here is the best news you will hear today: NO NEEDLES. This entire 8-week course uses nasal sprays only.\n\nYour protocol uses two complementary nootropic peptides: Semax for focus and cognitive enhancement, and Selank for calm, anxiety-free mental clarity. Together, they create a balanced state of sharp focus without the jitters or anxiety.\n\nSemax increases BDNF (brain-derived neurotrophic factor), enhancing attention, memory, and learning. Selank modulates GABA, reducing anxiety while maintaining mental clarity. The combination is synergistic—you get the cognitive boost without the overstimulation.\n\nThis course is perfect for anyone who wants cognitive enhancement without the commitment of daily injections. Two sprays each morning, and you are done.", "action_item": "Review your My Plan tab to understand your nasal spray protocol."},
    {"day": 1, "phase": "Introduction", "title": "Understanding Semax", "content": "Semax is a synthetic peptide derived from ACTH (adrenocorticotropic hormone). It was developed in Russia and has been used clinically there for decades for cognitive enhancement and neuroprotection.\n\nHow Semax works: It increases BDNF, a protein that supports the growth and maintenance of neurons. Higher BDNF levels are associated with better learning, memory, and cognitive function. Semax also modulates dopamine and serotonin systems, contributing to improved focus and mood.\n\nWhat to expect: Many people notice effects within the first few days—improved focus, better mental clarity, reduced brain fog. Effects are often subtle but cumulative. You may find yourself more productive, better at concentrating, and quicker at processing information.\n\nSemax has a mild stimulating effect, which is why we take it in the morning. It should not interfere with sleep when taken early in the day.", "action_item": "Read the Semax information in your My Plan tab and note any questions."},
    {"day": 2, "phase": "Introduction", "title": "Understanding Selank", "content": "Selank is the perfect complement to Semax. While Semax stimulates cognitive function, Selank provides calm focus by reducing anxiety without sedation.\n\nSelank works by modulating GABA, the brains primary calming neurotransmitter. Unlike benzodiazepines, which also work on GABA, Selank does not cause drowsiness or cognitive impairment. Instead, it produces a state of relaxed alertness.\n\nWhat to expect: Reduced anxiety and worry, better stress response, improved mood stability, and enhanced memory consolidation. Selank is particularly helpful for people who experience anxiety that interferes with their focus and productivity.\n\nThe combination of Semax plus Selank gives you cognitive enhancement (Semax) without the overstimulation or anxiety that can sometimes accompany stimulants (thanks to Selank). It is a balanced, sustainable approach to mental performance.", "action_item": "Review the Selank information in your My Plan tab."},
    {"day": 3, "phase": "Introduction", "title": "How to Use Nasal Sprays", "content": "Using nasal sprays is much simpler than injections. Here is how to do it properly:\n\nBefore first use: Prime the spray by pumping until a fine mist comes out (usually 2-3 pumps). This ensures you get a full dose on your first actual use.\n\nFor each dose: Clear your nasal passages (blow your nose if needed). Hold the spray bottle upright. Close one nostril, insert the tip into the other. Aim slightly outward (toward the outer wall of your nose). Press down firmly while breathing in gently. Hold your breath for a few seconds. Repeat for the other nostril if dose requires multiple sprays.\n\nStorage: Keep nasal sprays refrigerated for maximum stability. They can be kept at room temperature for short periods during travel.\n\nTiming: Take both Semax and Selank in the morning. You can take them one after another—no need to wait between them.", "action_item": "Practice the nasal spray technique with your bottles (priming if new)."},
    {"day": 4, "phase": "Introduction", "title": "Your First Doses", "content": "Today you begin your cognitive enhancement protocol. Your starting doses are: Semax: 200mcg (usually 1-2 sprays depending on concentration), and Selank: 250mcg (usually 1-2 sprays depending on concentration).\n\nMorning routine: After waking and getting ready, take your Semax spray first, then your Selank spray. You can take them back-to-back—no need to wait.\n\nWhat you might notice today: Semax can produce a sense of mental clarity or alertness within 15-30 minutes. Selank effects may be more subtle on day one but often include a calm, grounded feeling. Some people notice nothing significant on day one, and that is normal too.\n\nRemember: These are not dramatic stimulants. The effects are often described as feeling like your brain is working optimally rather than feeling drugged or altered.", "action_item": "Take your first doses of Semax and Selank this morning. Note the time and any effects."},
    {"day": 5, "phase": "Introduction", "title": "What to Notice", "content": "Now that you have had your first doses, start paying attention to subtle changes in your cognition. Things to track include: Focus duration—can you concentrate longer on tasks? Mental clarity—does thinking feel clearer or less foggy? Anxiety levels—are you less worried or stressed? Mood—do you feel more stable or positive? Memory—are you remembering things more easily?\n\nKeep a simple daily log. Rate each factor 1-10. Over time, patterns will emerge that show you how the peptides are affecting you.\n\nImportant: Effects are cumulative. Do not judge the protocol based on one or two days. Give it at least a week before assessing.", "action_item": "Create a simple daily cognitive tracking log (focus, clarity, anxiety, mood, memory 1-10)."},
    {"day": 6, "phase": "Introduction", "title": "Combining with Work and Study", "content": "The cognitive peptides work best when you give them something to enhance. Sitting idle will not show you their full potential.\n\nTo test your protocol: Engage in mentally demanding work during peak effect time (1-3 hours after dosing). Try learning something new—language, skill, concept. Do focused work without distractions. Notice if you can work longer before fatigue sets in.\n\nMany people find the peptides help most with: Sustained attention on difficult tasks, learning and retaining new information, working memory (holding multiple things in mind), and creative problem-solving.\n\nDo not just take the sprays and watch TV. Use them intentionally for meaningful cognitive work.", "action_item": "Schedule a focused work or study session for 1-2 hours after your morning dose tomorrow."},
    {"day": 7, "phase": "Introduction", "title": "Week 1 Complete", "content": "You have completed your first week of cognitive enhancement. Seven days of consistent nasal spray dosing—no needles, no complex protocols, just two sprays each morning.\n\nLet us assess: How has your focus been compared to before starting? Any reduction in anxiety or worry? Are you noticing clearer thinking? How easy has the routine been to maintain?\n\nAt this point, you are still on starting doses. Many people notice subtle improvements, but the real effects often become clearer in weeks 2-3, especially after we increase doses.\n\nContinue your current protocol for one more week before we increase.", "action_item": "Write a Week 1 summary: Focus, clarity, anxiety, and routine ease."},
    {"day": 8, "phase": "Building Effects", "title": "Week 2: Effects Building", "content": "Welcome to Week 2. Continue your starting doses: Semax 200mcg and Selank 250mcg, both in the morning.\n\nThis week, the peptides are building in your system. BDNF levels are increasing, GABA modulation is becoming more consistent. Many people notice more pronounced effects during Week 2.\n\nWatch for: Longer focus sessions without mental fatigue, reduced stress response to daily challenges, better recall of names, facts, and information, and improved verbal fluency (words coming more easily).\n\nIf you are not noticing much yet, do not worry. Some people are non-responders at lower doses and need the higher doses we will introduce in Week 3.", "action_item": "Continue tracking your cognitive metrics daily."},
    {"day": 9, "phase": "Building Effects", "title": "Optimizing Your Environment", "content": "Cognitive peptides work best in an optimized environment. Consider these factors:\n\nSleep: 7-9 hours is essential for cognitive function. Peptides enhance a well-rested brain; they cannot fix sleep deprivation. Nutrition: Your brain needs fuel—healthy fats, protein, and complex carbs. Consider omega-3s for brain health. Hydration: Even mild dehydration impairs cognition. Drink water throughout the day. Exercise: Physical activity boosts BDNF naturally, synergizing with Semax. Distraction management: Use focus tools—block distracting websites, use noise-canceling headphones, work in focused blocks.\n\nThe peptides are tools. They work best when everything else is optimized too.", "action_item": "Audit your sleep, nutrition, hydration, and exercise. Improve one factor this week."},
    {"day": 10, "phase": "Building Effects", "title": "The Stack Synergy", "content": "Semax and Selank are more powerful together than either alone. Here is why:\n\nSemax increases alertness and cognitive drive, but some people find it slightly stimulating. This can occasionally cause restlessness or difficulty relaxing.\n\nSelank provides anxiolytic effects that balance any overstimulation from Semax. It creates calm focus rather than jittery alertness.\n\nTogether, you get: Enhanced cognition without anxiety, better stress resilience, improved mood stability, and sustainable mental energy.\n\nThis is why we use both rather than just one. The combination is synergistic.", "action_item": "Note which peptide effects you notice more—the stimulation of Semax or the calm of Selank."},
    {"day": 11, "phase": "Building Effects", "title": "Cognitive Testing", "content": "Want to objectively measure your cognitive changes? Try these approaches:\n\nSubjective tracking: Daily log of focus, clarity, memory (1-10 scale). Objective tests: Free online tests for reaction time, working memory, and attention (search for cognitive assessment tools). Real-world metrics: Productivity measures—tasks completed, words written, problems solved. Learning speed: How quickly can you learn new information compared to before?\n\nHaving objective data helps you assess whether the protocol is working beyond just feeling better.", "action_item": "Take a baseline cognitive test online and note your scores for comparison later."},
    {"day": 12, "phase": "Building Effects", "title": "Managing Expectations", "content": "Let us be realistic about what cognitive peptides can and cannot do.\n\nThey can: Enhance focus and attention, reduce brain fog, improve memory consolidation, decrease anxiety without sedation, and support learning.\n\nThey cannot: Make you a genius overnight, replace sleep or good habits, fix serious cognitive issues (seek medical help for those), and give you photographic memory.\n\nThink of them as taking your cognition from 80% to 95%—not from 50% to 150%. They optimize what you have rather than giving you superhuman abilities.", "action_item": "Adjust your expectations if needed. Focus on realistic improvements."},
    {"day": 13, "phase": "Building Effects", "title": "Troubleshooting Common Issues", "content": "Some common issues and solutions:\n\nNot feeling anything: Some people need higher doses. Week 3 dose increase may help. Also ensure proper spray technique—are you actually getting the peptides into your nasal passages?\n\nToo stimulated: Take Semax earlier in the day, increase Selank dose slightly, or reduce Semax dose temporarily.\n\nNasal irritation: Use saline nasal spray to moisturize. Consider alternating nostrils.\n\nForgetfulness about dosing: Set a daily alarm, tie to existing habit (after brushing teeth, with morning coffee).\n\nIf issues persist, consult with a knowledgeable practitioner.", "action_item": "Identify any issues you are experiencing and apply the relevant solution."},
    {"day": 14, "phase": "Building Effects", "title": "Week 2 Complete", "content": "Two weeks of cognitive enhancement complete. Tomorrow, we increase your doses.\n\nAssess your progress: Compare your cognitive tracking to Week 1. Any improvements? How has the routine been?\n\nStarting tomorrow: Semax increases to 400mcg daily, Selank increases to 500mcg daily. This is the full protocol dose. Many people notice a significant jump in effects when moving to full doses.\n\nPrepare for the increase by ensuring you have enough supply and understanding your new spray counts.", "action_item": "Calculate how many sprays you will need for the increased doses tomorrow."},
    {"day": 15, "phase": "Dose Increase", "title": "Full Dose Protocol Begins", "content": "Welcome to your full dose protocol. Starting today: Semax: 400mcg daily (double your previous dose), Selank: 500mcg daily (double your previous dose).\n\nTake both in the morning as before. You may need more sprays depending on your bottles concentration. Check your product labeling.\n\nWhat to expect: More pronounced effects—clearer thinking, better focus, reduced anxiety. The transition should be smooth since you have 2 weeks of peptide exposure building tolerance.\n\nSome people notice the jump immediately. Others find it takes a few days at the new dose to feel the difference.", "action_item": "Take your first full doses this morning. Note any difference from lower doses."},
    {"day": 16, "phase": "Dose Increase", "title": "Maximizing Cognitive Sessions", "content": "At full doses, you should be experiencing peak cognitive enhancement. Make the most of it.\n\nPeak effect window: Usually 1-4 hours after dosing. Schedule your most demanding mental work during this time.\n\nStrategies for maximizing benefit: Do one big cognitively demanding task per day during peak. Use time-blocking—focused work in 25-50 minute blocks. Minimize context switching during peak hours. Save routine tasks for later in the day.\n\nYour brain on these peptides is primed for deep work. Do not waste it on email and social media.", "action_item": "Block 2-3 hours tomorrow morning for deep cognitive work."},
    {"day": 17, "phase": "Dose Increase", "title": "Learning and Memory", "content": "These peptides are particularly effective for learning and memory. Here is how to leverage this:\n\nSemax increases BDNF, which supports neuroplasticity—your brain ability to form new connections. This means learning new skills, languages, or information is enhanced.\n\nTo maximize learning: Study during peak effect hours. Use active recall (testing yourself) rather than passive review. Space your learning sessions (daily practice beats weekly cramming). Get good sleep—memory consolidation happens during sleep.\n\nIf you have been meaning to learn something new, now is the ideal time.", "action_item": "Choose one thing you want to learn and commit to daily practice during your cognitive window."},
    {"day": 18, "phase": "Dose Increase", "title": "Stress and Performance", "content": "Selank ability to reduce anxiety has significant performance benefits. Anxiety is one of the biggest cognitive performance killers.\n\nWhen you are anxious: Working memory decreases. Focus becomes scattered. Decision-making suffers. Learning is impaired.\n\nSelank helps by modulating GABA to reduce anxiety without sedation. This means you can approach challenging situations with calm confidence.\n\nNotice how you handle stress now vs. before starting. Do challenging tasks feel less overwhelming? Can you think clearly under pressure?", "action_item": "Pay attention to your stress response in challenging situations today."},
    {"day": 19, "phase": "Dose Increase", "title": "Week 3 Checkpoint", "content": "Three weeks complete, with full doses now established. Time for assessment.\n\nCompare to Week 1: Focus and concentration, mental clarity, anxiety levels, mood stability, and learning and memory. You should be seeing clearer benefits now at full doses.\n\nIf you are still not noticing effects: Ensure proper nasal spray technique. Consider if you might need higher doses (some people do). Rule out other factors affecting cognition (sleep, stress, etc.).", "action_item": "Complete a thorough Week 3 assessment in your log."},
    {"day": 20, "phase": "Dose Increase", "title": "Combining with Other Nootropics", "content": "Some people stack Semax and Selank with other cognitive enhancers. Common combinations include:\n\nSafe combinations: Caffeine plus L-theanine (balanced energy), omega-3 fatty acids (brain health support), racetams like piracetam (some people report synergy), and adaptogens like rhodiola (stress support).\n\nUse caution with: Other stimulants (can overstimulate with Semax), strong anxiolytics (may over-sedate with Selank), and prescription medications (consult a doctor).\n\nStart simple. You can experiment with additions later once you know how the base protocol affects you.", "action_item": "Evaluate whether any stack additions might benefit you (or if simple is best)."},
    {"day": 21, "phase": "Dose Increase", "title": "Week 3 Complete", "content": "Three weeks done—almost halfway through your course. You are now a week into full dosing.\n\nAt this point, you should have a clear sense of how these peptides affect you. Most people experience: Noticeably better focus and concentration, reduced anxiety and better stress handling, improved memory and recall, and more consistent mood and energy.\n\nThe next 5 weeks are about optimizing and maintaining these benefits while building sustainable cognitive habits.", "action_item": "Rate your overall cognitive improvement so far: 1-10 compared to baseline."},
    {"day": 22, "phase": "Dose Increase", "title": "Week 4: Optimization Begins", "content": "Welcome to the optimization phase. Your doses remain the same: Semax 400mcg, Selank 500mcg, both daily.\n\nThis week, focus on: Fine-tuning your timing for peak performance. Building habits that leverage your enhanced cognition. Identifying which tasks benefit most from the peptides. Creating a sustainable routine for the long term.", "action_item": "Identify the tasks where you notice the biggest cognitive benefit."},
    {"day": 23, "phase": "Dose Increase", "title": "Building Cognitive Habits", "content": "Enhanced cognition is most valuable when paired with good habits. Consider building:\n\nMorning routine: Dose your peptides, then 30-60 minutes of deep work before checking email or social media.\n\nLearning habit: 15-30 minutes daily of deliberate practice on a skill.\n\nReflection habit: End of day review of what you learned and accomplished.\n\nThe peptides make these habits easier to maintain and more effective. Use this window to build systems that will serve you long-term.", "action_item": "Choose one cognitive habit to build this week."},
    {"day": 24, "phase": "Dose Increase", "title": "Cognitive Endurance", "content": "One benefit you may be noticing is cognitive endurance—the ability to maintain focus and mental performance over longer periods.\n\nBefore peptides, you might have hit a wall after 2-3 hours of focused work. Now you may be able to sustain focus for 4-5 hours or more.\n\nLeverage this: Schedule longer deep work sessions. Tackle complex projects that require sustained attention. Learn difficult subjects that previously felt overwhelming.\n\nBut also respect your limits. Even enhanced cognition needs rest.", "action_item": "Try an extended focused work session (3+ hours) and note how you feel."},
    {"day": 25, "phase": "Dose Increase", "title": "Social and Verbal Benefits", "content": "Some people notice improved social cognition on Semax and Selank: Words coming more easily (verbal fluency), better reading of social situations, reduced social anxiety (Selank), and more engaging in conversations.\n\nIf you notice these benefits, leverage them: Have important conversations during your peak window. Practice public speaking or presentations. Engage in networking or social events.\n\nNot everyone notices social benefits, and that is okay. The primary effects are cognitive.", "action_item": "Pay attention to any social or verbal improvements you are experiencing."},
    {"day": 26, "phase": "Dose Increase", "title": "Week 4 Checkpoint", "content": "Four weeks complete. Halfway through your course.\n\nMajor checkpoint assessment: What specific cognitive improvements have you noticed? How has your productivity changed? Any anxiety or mood benefits? Is the routine sustainable? Are you using the cognitive enhancement for meaningful work?\n\nYou have 4 weeks remaining. Use them to solidify benefits and plan for post-course.", "action_item": "Complete a comprehensive Week 4 assessment."},
    {"day": 27, "phase": "Dose Increase", "title": "The Compound Effect", "content": "The benefits of cognitive enhancement compound over time. Here is how:\n\nBetter focus leads to: More productive work, faster learning, better decisions. These lead to: Improved outcomes, more confidence, reduced stress. Which creates: A positive cycle of cognitive and life improvement.\n\nThe 8 weeks of this course are not just about temporary enhancement. They are about creating patterns of high performance that can persist.", "action_item": "Identify one area where you have seen compound benefits."},
    {"day": 28, "phase": "Dose Increase", "title": "Week 4 Complete", "content": "One month done. Four weeks of cognitive enhancement under your belt.\n\nYou have established: A consistent daily routine, full dose protocol effectiveness, habits that leverage enhanced cognition, and a baseline of improved performance.\n\nThe second half of your course is about sustaining and optimizing these gains while preparing for long-term cognitive health.", "action_item": "Celebrate one month of consistency. Note your biggest win so far."},
    {"day": 29, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Second Half Begins", "content": "Welcome to the second half of your Cognitive Enhancement Course. Weeks 5-8 focus on optimization and sustainability.\n\nYour protocol remains the same: Semax 400mcg daily, Selank 500mcg daily. By now, this should feel like second nature.\n\nThis phase focuses on: Maximizing the benefits you are getting, building sustainable cognitive habits, planning for long-term use or cycling, and integrating enhanced cognition into your life goals.", "action_item": "Set 2-3 cognitive or productivity goals for the next 4 weeks."},
    {"day": 30, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Productivity Systems", "content": "With enhanced cognition, now is the time to level up your productivity systems.\n\nConsider implementing: Time blocking—schedule focused work, not just meetings. Task management—capture everything, prioritize ruthlessly. Deep work rituals—consistent triggers for focused states. Energy management—align demanding tasks with your peak hours.\n\nThe peptides give you raw cognitive power. Systems help you direct that power effectively.", "action_item": "Choose one productivity system to implement or improve this week."},
    {"day": 31, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Creative Work", "content": "Cognitive peptides can enhance creative work as well as analytical tasks.\n\nSemax and BDNF support the formation of new neural connections, which is essential for creativity—making novel associations between ideas.\n\nSelank reduces the anxiety that often blocks creative expression. When you are not worried about judgment, creativity flows more freely.\n\nExperiment with: Writing, brainstorming, design work, music, problem-solving requiring novel solutions.\n\nYou may find your creative output is enhanced during peak cognitive hours.", "action_item": "Try a creative task during your peak cognitive window and note the results."},
    {"day": 32, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Long-term Planning", "content": "Start thinking about what comes after this 8-week course.\n\nOptions include:\n\nContinued daily use: Many people use Semax and Selank indefinitely with good results.\n\nCycling: 4-8 weeks on, 2-4 weeks off. This may help maintain sensitivity.\n\nAs-needed use: Using only during demanding cognitive periods (exams, projects, etc.).\n\nLower maintenance dose: Reducing to the starting doses for sustained mild enhancement.\n\nThere is no established optimal approach. Experiment to find what works for you.", "action_item": "Research long-term use strategies and start forming your post-course plan."},
    {"day": 33, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Week 5 Checkpoint", "content": "Five weeks complete. Three weeks remaining.\n\nCheck in: Are cognitive benefits sustained at full strength? Any tolerance building (feeling less effect)? How is the routine—still consistent? Are you leveraging enhancement for meaningful goals?\n\nIf you notice tolerance: Some people take weekend breaks. Others alternate peptides. Consult with a practitioner if concerned.", "action_item": "Complete Week 5 assessment and note any tolerance concerns."},
    {"day": 34, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Brain Health Beyond Peptides", "content": "Cognitive peptides work best as part of overall brain health. Long-term strategies include:\n\nPhysical exercise: Perhaps the most powerful cognitive enhancer. 30+ minutes of cardio increases BDNF naturally.\n\nSleep optimization: 7-9 hours consistently. Sleep is when memory consolidates.\n\nNutrition: Mediterranean diet, omega-3s, and antioxidants support brain health.\n\nCognitive challenges: Keep learning new things to maintain neuroplasticity.\n\nSocial connection: Social engagement protects cognitive function.\n\nStress management: Chronic stress damages the brain. Meditation, nature, and downtime help.\n\nThese factors compound with peptides for optimal results.", "action_item": "Rate yourself 1-10 on each brain health factor. Improve your lowest."},
    {"day": 35, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Week 5 Complete", "content": "Five weeks done. Two and a half weeks remaining.\n\nYou are in the home stretch. The habits and benefits you have built over 5 weeks should feel natural now.\n\nContinue your protocol: Semax 400mcg daily, Selank 500mcg daily. Keep leveraging your enhanced cognition for meaningful work and goals.", "action_item": "Reflect on the transformation from Week 1 to now."},
    {"day": 36, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Week 6: Consolidation", "content": "This week is about consolidating your gains. The cognitive improvements you have experienced should feel consistent and reliable now.\n\nFocus on: Maintaining your routine with zero friction, using enhanced cognition for your most important goals, building habits that will persist post-course, and documenting what works best for you.", "action_item": "Identify which aspects of your enhanced cognition you want to maintain long-term."},
    {"day": 37, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Teaching and Sharing", "content": "One way to solidify what you have learned is to teach it to others.\n\nConsider: Sharing your experience with friends interested in cognitive enhancement. Documenting your protocol and results. Writing about what you have learned.\n\nTeaching forces you to clarify your understanding and creates lasting knowledge structures in your brain.", "action_item": "Explain your cognitive enhancement journey to someone (or write it for yourself)."},
    {"day": 38, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Stress Testing", "content": "How do you perform under stress on this protocol?\n\nTest yourself: Take on a challenging deadline. Have a difficult conversation. Face a situation that would normally cause anxiety.\n\nSelank benefits should shine here—reduced anxiety and better stress response while maintaining cognitive clarity.\n\nNote how you perform under pressure compared to before starting the protocol.", "action_item": "Identify an upcoming stressful situation to observe your enhanced stress response."},
    {"day": 39, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Week 6 Checkpoint", "content": "Six weeks complete. Two weeks remaining.\n\nAssessment: Cognitive improvements—sustained, improved, or plateaued? Anxiety and mood—still benefiting? Routine—running smoothly? Goals—making progress on what matters?\n\nThe final two weeks are about finishing strong and transitioning to your long-term plan.", "action_item": "Complete Week 6 assessment."},
    {"day": 40, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Reflecting on Change", "content": "Take time to reflect on how you have changed over 6 weeks.\n\nCognitive changes: Better focus, clarity, memory? Emotional changes: Reduced anxiety, improved mood? Behavioral changes: New habits, better productivity? Life changes: Progress on goals, improved outcomes?\n\nThese changes are real. The peptides helped, but your consistent effort made them happen.", "action_item": "Write a reflection on your transformation over 6 weeks."},
    {"day": 41, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Post-Course Planning", "content": "In two weeks, your course ends. Finalize your post-course plan:\n\nOption A: Continue at full doses—order more supplies.\n\nOption B: Reduce to starting doses for maintenance.\n\nOption C: Cycle—take 2-4 weeks off, then run another course.\n\nOption D: Stop and observe how cognition changes without peptides.\n\nThere is no wrong answer. Choose what fits your goals and situation.", "action_item": "Finalize and write down your post-course plan."},
    {"day": 42, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Week 6 Complete", "content": "Six weeks done. One and a half weeks remaining.\n\nYou have maintained a consistent cognitive enhancement protocol for 6 weeks. That is 42 days of enhanced focus, clarity, and reduced anxiety.\n\nThe final 2 weeks are about finishing with intention and setting yourself up for long-term success.", "action_item": "Celebrate six weeks of consistency."},
    {"day": 43, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Week 7: Finishing Strong", "content": "Your final full week begins. Continue your protocol: Semax 400mcg daily, Selank 500mcg daily.\n\nThis week, focus on: Using enhanced cognition for your biggest remaining goals, solidifying habits you want to maintain, preparing for post-course transition, and documenting final results.", "action_item": "Identify one big goal to accomplish this week."},
    {"day": 44, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "What You Have Accomplished", "content": "Take stock of everything you have achieved over 7 weeks:\n\nDays of consistent dosing: 44 and counting. New habits built: List them. Goals achieved: List them. Cognitive improvements: Rate compared to baseline. Anxiety improvements: Rate compared to baseline.\n\nThis is significant. You committed to cognitive enhancement and followed through.", "action_item": "List every accomplishment and improvement from this course."},
    {"day": 45, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Sustainable Practices", "content": "Which practices from this course will you sustain long-term?\n\nCandidates: Morning cognitive work sessions, learning and memory practices, stress management techniques, brain health habits (exercise, sleep, nutrition), and productivity systems.\n\nThe peptides may or may not continue, but these practices should. They are the foundation of long-term cognitive health.", "action_item": "Choose 3-5 practices to sustain beyond this course."},
    {"day": 46, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Week 7 Checkpoint", "content": "Seven weeks complete. One week remaining.\n\nFinal check-in: Have cognitive benefits remained strong through Week 7? Are you ready for post-course transition? Have you ordered supplies if continuing? Do you have a clear plan for what comes next?\n\nOne more week to finish your course with intention.", "action_item": "Complete Week 7 assessment. Confirm post-course plan."},
    {"day": 47, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Gratitude and Growth", "content": "Take a moment for gratitude. You invested in your cognitive health. You committed to 8 weeks of consistent effort. You learned about your brain and how to optimize it.\n\nGrowth mindset reminder: Cognitive enhancement is ongoing. This course is a step, not a destination. Continue learning, experimenting, and growing.", "action_item": "Write three things you are grateful for about this cognitive enhancement journey."},
    {"day": 48, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Final Week Prep", "content": "One week remaining. Prepare for a strong finish.\n\nInventory: Check remaining peptide supply—use it all. Goals: Any final goals to accomplish with enhanced cognition? Documentation: Prepare your final assessment. Transition: Mentally prepare for post-course routine.", "action_item": "Plan your final week to finish strong."},
    {"day": 49, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Week 7 Complete", "content": "Seven weeks done. One week left.\n\nYou are in the final stretch of your Cognitive Enhancement Course. 49 days of nasal spray dosing, enhanced focus, reduced anxiety, and improved cognitive performance.\n\nMake your last week count.", "action_item": "Commit to perfect consistency for the final week."},
    {"day": 50, "phase": "Optimization", "title": "Final Week Begins", "content": "Your final week of the Cognitive Enhancement Course begins.\n\nContinue: Semax 400mcg daily, Selank 500mcg daily.\n\nThis week, focus on: Completing any remaining goals, final documentation and assessment, using remaining supplies, and celebrating your achievement.", "action_item": "Use your enhanced cognition for your most important task today."},
